prince harry is back in the uk for a  very special occasion  a source tells et the 36 year old royal  has safely arrived in his home country  for the unveiling of the statue of his  late mother princess diana  well of course this event in july is is  much anticipated  the unveiling of the diamond statue is  going to be an  important date it's firmly cemented in  both of the brothers calendars  harry and his brother prince william are  set to attend a small event to mark the  unveiling of a statue they commissioned  of their mother in the sunken garden at  kensington palace on july  1 a day which would have been diana's  60th birthday  i think everyone is hoping that we will  see the brothers  shoulder by shoulder to unveil that  statue in memory of their mother diana  always said to them  always stay close don't ever fall out  she would be devastated that that is  what's happened  and she would be wanting them to feed  her together for that unveiling of the  statue in her honor  a source tells et harry is now at  frogmore cottage  the windsor residence where he and his  wife meghan markle lived before stepping  away from their royal roles  the source adds prince harry will land  in the uk and  isolate for five days before taking a  covet test  affirming that he is negative before the  events of the day  a source also previously told et that  megan will not attend the unveiling of  the statue  seeing as she just gave birth to their  daughter lillabet diana  earlier this month meanwhile royal  expert katie nicholl told et in april  that while harry and william still have  a long way to go when it comes to  repairing their relationship  the unveiling of the statue of their  late mother is a significant event  things were not going to be resolved in  in one or two family meetings so while  this has been an important  step i think there's still quite a way  to go  the idea that harry's suddenly going to  come around to william's way of thinking  and vice versa  i think is is a way off i think there do  need to be  more conversations there's clearly still  a lot of hurt  a lot of resentment and a degree of  mistrust  i think on both parts harry was last in  the uk  in april to attend the funeral of his  grandfather prince philip  at the windsor castle ceremony he was  seen with other members of the royal  family  including prince charles his brother  william and duchess kate  for the first time since he and megan  stepped away from their formal roles in  the monarchy  so it's early days but i think the hope  is that come july when we are hoping to  see the brothers  stand once again shoulder by shoulder to  unveil  the statue in memory of their mother  that the relationship will be  stronger and in a better place
 

